PATCH 390: fix the AZER2 mission crash at FUN_0000_c7ca+0x5c (SIGSEGV fault-addr 0x2001a) -- the next
"twin" after patch 389's 2004 fix -- and reconstruct its base-lost callee FUN_0000_c3ed.

Runtime-captured (setarch -R, FIST_SEGV_BT/EBP/MGA, commit a0bccac): fault EIP 0x08082eb5 = c7ca+0x5c,
param_2(obj)=0x00020004 (a STALE arg, NOT a base-loss of a real ptr); EBP chain app_entry->00d0->cae6->
e714->459a->22dd->378e->c33c->c4df->c7ca.  So c7ca is a per-object cockpit render method dispatched
ARG-LESS by c4df (asm c551 `call *%gs:0x3632(%bx)`, obj in SI) -> ALL its __allregs params are stale
garbage.  This is the c681/patch-310 arg-less-render class, NOT the c68c/389 caller-base-loss class.

c7ca asm 0xc7ca-0x816 (DS=DGROUP=0x1c00): obj=SI (c4df publishes it in g_fist_render_si); gate testw
0x1,[0x6d2c]; skip iff !(2dab&2)&&(obj[0x16]&8)&&obj[0x36]==0; else c3ed(obj), bx=((obj[0x26]+0x400)>>8)&
0xf8, +0x10d8/+0x11d8 & ah=0x24/0x0e by obj[0x16]&8, ah=0 if obj[0x1c], c8c2(ax,bx,BP,obj,0).  Ghidra
deref'd the obj (param_2) as a host ptr -> wild read.  Rebased every obj deref to dg+si and threaded the
x86 CF via g_fist_cf (skip=1 -> c4df next object; render returns CF=0 [c8c2's clc] -> c4df yields).  Twin
of c584 (patch 321).  c8c2's obj arg is the NEAR offset (ca2f does dg+(uint16)param_4); [di+0x1a]=BP is
untraced (not set in 378e/c33c/c4df, sibling c681->c962 passes 0, field outside the central-chrome crop)
-> passed 0, to be pinned once a mission-cockpit-azer2 oracle exists.

c3ed (asm 0xc3ed-0x47c) was ALSO base-lost (first reached via c7ca): it appends 6 {word,word,tag} records
from obj[0x6e..0x85] (tags 'E'0x45..'@'0x40) into STRSEG:[a6e2] (GS=word[DGROUP:0x70]=STRSEG; a6e2 = a
WORD near offset into STRSEG, inited 0x31ca by c3dc, advanced +30).  Ghidra deref'd param_1(obj) and the
a6e2 cursor as host pointers.  Its AX return is discarded by c8c2 (which sets al=0x10) -> side-effect only.
Also retype DAT_2000_a6e2 undefined2 (WORD, not int**): the 4-byte type overlapped a6e4 AND was the vehicle
for the host-ptr deref; a6e4 is already undefined2.  Blast radius = c3dc(init)/c3ed(rewritten)/c47d(compare)
only; on type-0/M1 maps (AZER1/CYPRUS1) the a6e2 buffer stays empty (a6e4==a6e2) so c47d is a no-op ->
behaviour-neutral for the 3 bit-verified mission flows (which never reach c7ca/c3ed: they are type-0/M1).

VALIDATED: AZER1 + CYPRUS1 + mission-cockpit central-chrome AE=0 unchanged (no regression); AZER2 advances
past c7ca.  Engine re_out/fist.c stays pristine.  All asm-verified vs re_out/fist_dat_image.bin.

